# ─── Job Fair frontend — REMOTE environment template ───────────────
# The shape of a DEPLOYED frontend. Set these in Coolify's environment
# variables for the service.
#
# Also copy this file to .env when you want the LOCAL frontend to run
# against the deployed backend — that is the supported way to switch
# targets, rather than editing .env.local.example's values.
#
# BUILD-TIME: Vite inlines VITE_* at build time, so changing one on the
# host requires a REDEPLOY — restarting the service is not enough, and
# they must be set as BUILD variables, not runtime ones.
#
# VITE_* values are exposed to the browser. Never put a secret here.

# ─── Mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of: local | demo | prod.
# `demo` is a first-class mode, not a flavour of prod: a demo deploy
# points at demo data and must stay visibly distinguishable from the
# real form, so demo submissions are never mistaken for real applicants.
VITE_APP_MODE=prod

# ─── API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO trailing slash — `${API_URL}/applicants` would become
# `//applicants`, which many routers 404. The previous value had one.
#
# There is deliberately no fallback host in src/config/api.js: a
# production build with this unset throws at startup rather than
# silently calling a decommissioned server.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.form.amxr.site
